<title>USA: IPO FILING-Endocardial Solutions Inc.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING-Endocardial Solutions Inc.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		 Endocardial Solutions Inc</p>
<p>Stock symbol			ECSI.O</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   $10-$12/shr</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    3.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company *     3.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    8,759,031</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Piper Jaffray Inc</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  450,000 shrs</p>
<p>* - Of the 3 million common, Endocardial intends to sell up to 750,000 to Medtronic Inc, an existing shareholder.  </p>
<p>Business: St. Paul, Minn., company designs, develops, and manufactures a minimally invasive diagnostic system that diagnoses, within the span of a few heartbeats, tachycardia, a potentially fatal abnormal heart rhythm.</p>
<p>Use of Proceeds: Continued development and testing of, and clinical trials for, the EnSite System, capital expenditures, research and development, manufacturing and marketing activities, and working capital and other general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Financial Data in 000s year ended Dec 31:</p>
<p>				   1996		 1995</p>
<p>   - Revenue		     N/A		 N/A</p>
<p>   - Net Income  (loss)  ($6,481)	  ($4,734)</p>
